{"kind":"request","text":"codex: design the write-boundary guards for the two recurring breakdown families of 2026-08-25/26, at hugh direction (given in session, recorded here): skip convention amendments and fix these in tooling. Design only; implementation goes to child requests on then-current bases. FAMILY ONE, verdict filed past unread head-news. Twice tonight a reviewer approved an exact head while durable corrections naming that head sat unaddressed (receipt approval over codex blockers at 0608526d; UI approval over the two 3fd75543 blockers), and each cost an unwind cycle. Design a gs review preflight — and the same check in the MCP review path via internal/reviewguard — that enumerates durable records citing the exact reviewed head filed after the review promise, and refuses or requires explicit acknowledgment of each uncited one in the verdict. Decide refusal versus acknowledgment, the citation-matching rule (full-id, head-hash, or path@commit), and how the guard composes with the existing reviewguard checks. FAMILY TWO, malformed or doomed durable writes accepted silently. Tonight produced: a hand-filed verdict without body.artifact that blocked a merge; verdicts filed as plain reports outside gs review needing canonical refiles; a ratification filed as gs state --kind ratify landing as undefined-kind with no edge; and repeated stale-at-birth filings where the writer had only a warning note on stderr. Design the write-boundary treatment for each: an undefined kind refuses with a pointer to the defined command; a body shaped like a verdict (body.verdict or body.status carrying approved/changes-requested) outside gs review refuses with a pointer to gs review; a rests_on entry that is retired or stale at admission requires an explicit override flag (name it) instead of a passive note, with the override recorded in the act body so readers see it was chosen. State for each guard: enforcement site (CLI, MCP adapter, fold admission, or resident), whether it is refusal or flagged override, compatibility for existing history and replays, and the test surface. Keep the guards advisory-shaped where refusal would break lawful rare cases, and refusal-shaped where tonight showed no lawful case.","body":{"conditions":"A design ruling covering both families: head-news preflight for gs review and the MCP review path with its matching and acknowledgment rules; write-boundary treatment for undefined kinds, verdict-shaped bodies outside gs review, and dead-or-stale rests_on with a named recorded override; enforcement site, refusal-versus-override choice, history/replay compatibility, and test surface stated per guard; no implementation under this request — child implementation requests on then-current bases.","severity":"medium","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}